Market risk changes prices; credit risk changes repayment; liquidity risk impedes funding or sale; operational risk arises from failed processes.|A borrower defaults while a trading system fails: distinct risks interact.|One risk metric covers all these exposures adequately?|No|Yes|Only VaR
Strategic, business, and reputational risks affect demand, positioning, and trust.|A misconduct incident triggers customer departures and funding pressure.|Reputational losses can affect cash flows?|Yes|No|Only after fines
Counterparty risk concerns contract failure; settlement risk concerns exchanging obligations as planned.|One currency is paid before the other currency is received.|This creates…?|Settlement exposure|Only inventory exposure|Only dividend risk
Concentration amplifies shared exposure; contagion transmits stress across connected participants.|Many borrowers depend on one commodity despite different company names.|Borrower count alone proves diversification?|No|Yes|Only above 100 loans
VaR is a loss quantile at specified horizon/confidence; expected shortfall averages losses in the relevant tail.|A 99% one-day VaR does not describe every loss beyond its threshold.|VaR is the maximum possible loss?|No|Yes|Only at 99%
Historical, parametric, and Monte Carlo risk methods use different data and distribution assumptions.|Normal-model VaR may miss heavy tails.|Method choice removes input uncertainty?|No|Yes|Only simulation
Stress testing evaluates adverse conditions; reverse stress asks what could break the business.|Find the withdrawal rate that exhausts a bank's usable liquidity.|This is…?|Reverse stress testing|Only a base forecast|A guaranteed prediction
Scenarios combine plausible shocks with mechanisms and time horizons.|Recession lowers sales, raises defaults, and tightens funding.|Independent random input changes always make coherent scenarios?|No|Yes|Only with many inputs
Risk appetite states acceptable exposure; limits operationalise it; governance assigns accountability.|A concentration cap triggers review when breached.|A limit without monitoring and enforcement is…?|Incomplete control|Guaranteed protection|A valuation method
Credit portfolio risk depends on individual losses, dependence, concentration, and common drivers.|Defaults rise together during a sector downturn.|Independent-default assumptions can understate…?|Joint tail losses|Only coupon income|Only loan count
AL mismatches include maturity, repricing, currency, and liquidity differences.|Long-term illiquid assets are funded with overnight borrowing.|Main vulnerability?|Rollover and funding stress|Only tax depreciation|Only market share
Model risk arises from incorrect design, inputs, use, or implementation; validation challenges each.|A well-coded model uses an inappropriate distribution.|Code correctness proves model adequacy?|No|Yes|Only after backtesting
Operational and cyber risks include fraud, outage, error, and information compromise.|Payment-system downtime delays settlements and creates losses.|Cyber risk is only an IT issue with no financial effect?|No|Yes|Only before insurance
ERM coordinates risks across the organisation and strategy rather than treating silos independently.|A supply shock affects sales, FX, credit, and funding simultaneously.|ERM should examine…?|Interactions and response capacity|Only separate risk lists|Only insurance premiums
Economic capital estimates loss-absorbing needs under a chosen confidence framework; RAROC compares return with risk capital.|₹5 risk-adjusted profit over ₹50 allocated capital gives 10%.|RAROC equals raw revenue growth?|No|Yes|Only for banks
Systemic risk threatens broader financial functioning through leverage, runs, common shocks, and interconnectedness.|Forced asset sales depress prices and trigger further margin calls.|This illustrates…?|A feedback loop|Perfect market stability|Only individual negligence
